insight:
Here is a modified version of the script to include the desired parameters:



  const targetURL = "https://example.com/?name=John&email=john@gmail.com&phone=1234567";
  window.location.href = targetURL;


This script uses the const keyword to declare a constant variable called targetURL, which contains the specified URL with the parameters appended to it. Then, the window.location.href property is assigned to the targetURL variable to perform the redirect to the specified URL.


To pass multiple parameters, you can separate each parameter with an ampersand &, as shown in `&email=john@gmail.com&phone=1234567`
